  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many more acorns each squirrel needs to collect, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of acorns needed for all 5 squirrels to get through the winter.\n2. Subtract the number of acorns already collected from the total number of acorns needed.\n3. Divide the remaining number of acorns by the number of squirrels to find out how many more acorns each squirrel needs to collect.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. The total number of acorns needed for all 5 squirrels is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 130 = 650\n   \\]\n\n2. The number of acorns already collected by the 5 squirrels is 575. The number of acorns still needed is:\n   \\[\n   650 - 575 = 75\n   \\]\n\n3. The number of acorns each squirrel still needs to collect is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{75}{5} = 15\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, each squirrel needs to collect \\(\\boxed{15}\\) more acorns.",
